## §4 verdict on post-hoc 4's prose claim
  Post-hoc 4 said the 23 -> 44 gap is "expected and is NOT a defect".
  Published sites at the arm commit: 23
  Sites at HEAD whose file ALREADY EXISTED at the arm commit: 27
  delta (AT-RISK − published): +4

  REFUTED IN PART — 4 site(s) lived in files that existed when the arm ran and are
  not covered by the published 23. "Different commits" does not account for those. They are
  either sites the arm missed, or sites ADDED to pre-existing files after the arm ran —
  which this key cannot tell apart, because it keys on FILE existence, not LINE existence.
  Stated as the limit it is: this partition prices the gap, it does not attribute it.

## §5 the limit of this reconciliation, stated before anyone cites it
  Keying on file existence CANNOT separate "the arm missed a site" from "a site was appended
  to an old file afterwards". A line-level reconciliation would need the arm-commit blob of
  every AT-RISK file re-scanned with the same key. That is the next rung and it is NOT driven
  here — named, unblocked, not claimed as done.
